ps://api.github.com/repos/junit-team/junit-framework/issues/comments/227000446","html_url":"https://github.com/junit-team/junit-framework/issues/318#issuecomment-227000446","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/junit-team/junit-framework/issues/318","id":227000446,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDIyNzAwMDQ0Ng==","user":{"login":"sbrannen","id":104798,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwNDc5OA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/104798?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sbrannen","html_url":"https://github.com/sbrannen","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sbrannen/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sbrannen/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sbrannen/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sbrannen/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sbrannen/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sbrannen/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sbrannen/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sbrannen/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sbrannen/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2016-06-19T14:32:03Z","updated_at":"2016-06-19T14:39:48Z","body":"I agree with both of you:\n1. The way it's implemented now in JUnit Jupiter seems logical, natural.\n2. However, it's not how JUnit 4, Hamcrest, or AssertJ do it.\n   - Presumably other assertion frameworks forego identity checks as well, but I didn't investigate further.\n3. As @sormuras pointed out, one should invoke `assertSame` if one is interested in checking for identity.\n\nSo, in summary, we will revert the behavior in JUnit Jupiter to align with JUnit 4, AssertJ, etc.\n","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/junit-team/junit-framework/issues/comments/227000446/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh"